non-existent Python API method, the bridge handles it poorly and can lock up the UI on rapid navigation. Methods must perfectly match `backend.py`.\n- **Window Management**: `API.on_closing(self)` in `backend.py` handles the `window.events.closing` hook but it only shuts down the MSEMAX server; it does *not* call `self.window.destroy()`. That's why the JS `exitApp()` function doesn't actually close the window.\n- **Server Subprocess**: `MSEMAXServerManager` in `server_manager.py` now accepts a `logger_callback` and spawns a background thread to read the server's output pipe.\n- **Drag & Drop**: Pywebview natively supports file dropping via the `window.events.dropped` hook in python, which passes a list of file paths. We can intercept this in `app.py` and pass it to the frontend via `evaluate_js`.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Files and Code\n\n### Edited Files\n- **`d:\\AI_Engineer\\Pharmacy-agy\\desktop_app\\templates\\index.html`**\n  - *What:* Fixed `is_server_running` JS calls to `get_server_status`. Added CSS animations, background patterns, and shadows.\n- **`d:\\AI_Engineer\\Pharmacy-agy\\desktop_app\\server_manager.py`**\n  - *What:* Modified `MSEMAXServerManager.__init__` to accept a `logger_callback`. Piped `stdout/stderr` in the `start()` method and spawned a `_read_output` background thread to capture server logs.\n\n### Viewed Files\n- **`d:\\AI_Engineer\\Pharmacy-agy\\desktop_app\\backend.py`**\n  - *File Landscape:* Defines the `API` class exposed to JS. Initializes `MSEMAXServerManager`.\n  - *Relevance:* Needs to be updated to pass a log callback to the server manager, hold an internal list of logs, and expose a `get_logs()` method to JS. Also needs an `exit_app` method to actually destroy the window.\n- **`d:\\AI_Engineer\\Pharmacy-agy\\desktop_app\\app.py`**\n  - *File Landscape:* Pywebview initialization entry point.\n  - *Relevance:* Needs to be updated to handle `window.events.dropped` for the drag-and-drop feature.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Current Work and Next Steps\n\n**Current Status:** The user explicitly requested an Exit button fix, drag-and-drop file support, and a visible log viewer in the Settings UI. I have just modified `server_manager.py` to capture logs, but haven't hooked it up to the frontend yet.\n\n**Next Steps for the Next Agent:**\n\n1. **Implement the Log System (backend)**\n   - Open `d:\\AI_Engineer\\Pharmacy-agy\\desktop_app\\backend.py`.\n   - Add `self.logs = []` to the `API` class. Add a `def log(self, message: str)` method that appends to `self.logs`.\n   - Update `self.server_manager = MSEMAXServerManager(..., logger_callback=self.log)`.\n   - Add a `get_logs(self)` method to return the logs to JS.\n\n2. **Implement the Log Viewer (frontend)**\n   - Open `d:\\AI_Engineer\\Pharmacy-agy\\desktop_app\\templates\\index.html`.\n   - Add a terminal-like `<div id=\"log-viewer\">` in the Settings screen section.\n   - Add a JS `setInterval` to fetch `get_logs()` and populate the viewer so the user can see the server/app output in real-time.\n\n3. **Fix the Exit Button**\n   - In `backend.py`, add `def exit_app(self): if self.window: self.window.destroy()`.\n   - In `index.html`, update the `exitApp()` JS function to call `window.pywebview.api.exit_app()`.\n\n4. **Implement Drag and Drop**\n   - In `d:\\AI_Engineer\\Pharmacy-agy\\desktop_app\\app.py`, hook `window.events.dropped += on_drop`.\n   - Write `on_drop(files)` to use `window.evaluate_js` to send the dropped file paths into the JS context (so they can be added to the warehouse/shortage lists). Alternatively, implement HTML5 drag-and-drop listeners inside `index.html`.\n\nYou have the 12 following artifacts written to the artifacts directory:\n\n[ARTIFACT: agent]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/kakak/.gemini/antigravity/brain/916274de-7f92-49fc-a0a8-d291664b474a/.agents/agents/desktop-builder/agent.md\nLast Edited: 2026-09-21T22:17:02Z\n\n[ARTIFACT: agent]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/kakak/.gemini/antigravity/brain/916274de-7f92-49fc-a0a8-d291664b474a/.agents/ag